; Room state: what the main loop does next
;
; The main loop #R$85FC takes the low 7 bits: 1 = enter the room #R$8509 (#R$86B9); 2 = put the player at the respawn
; position ($8512/$8514), then enter the room (set by the passage items #R$A6BC/#R$A6D8); 3 = ending sequence #R$887B
; (set by the red scroll in Satan's room, #R$A668); 4 = restore the last checkpoint (#R$BDF3), then as 2 (set to $84 by
; the end of the dying animation #R$AA99 when lives are left); 5 = Game Over screen (#R$AA99 makes it $85 when no life
; is left; both abort keys, #R$A596); 0 or anything above 5: run the frame routines. Bit 7 keeps the frame routines
; (player, entities, drawing) running: the loop sets the state to $80 after a room has been entered. #R$9C52 and the
; cutscene loop clear and restore it so that the frame update stops while a parchment is shown. The room-entry code
; #R$86B9 clears it.
@label=RoomState
g$850C DEFB $00
